\newlabel{fig:correlation_heatmap}{{8}{7}{Pearson $r$ by contamination estimator and model size. Per-model-size correlations all exceed $r = 0.5$ (160M: $r=0.631$; 410M: $r=0.799$; 1B: $r=0.539$; 6.9B: $r=0.856$), with larger models trending toward stronger signal}{figure.8}{}}
